/*
 * cascade_input_preserve.gq -- --dump-leds golden CSV fixture for
 * gamequeer#455: load_stage() used to unconditionally clear EVERY pending
 * event bit (including user-input events: BUTTON_A/B/L/R, BUTTON_CLICK) on
 * every stage load. Combined with GQ_OP_GOSTAGE calling load_stage()
 * synchronously mid-dispatch, and handle_events()'s single forward pass
 * over event_type 0 (ENTER) .. GQ_EVENT_COUNT, this meant: if a stage's own
 * `enter` event auto-cascades into another stage via `gostage` (no timer,
 * no user action -- purely a same-tick chain), any button/dial event
 * HAL_event_poll() already OR'd into s_gq_event *that same tick* -- before
 * handle_events() reached its index in the loop -- was silently wiped by
 * the cascade's load_stage() call and never dispatched to the destination
 * stage. See gamequeer#455's diagnosis for the full trace and the
 * hardware-observed symptom (first dial turn after an auto-cascading boot
 * chain does nothing).
 *
 * Two stages, no scripted navigation beyond one input token landing on the
 * cascade tick itself:
 *
 *   boot: `event enter { gostage idle; }` -- an immediate, unconditional
 *         cascade with no timer and no button involved, so it fires on
 *         tick 0, inside the very first handle_events() pass (ENTER is
 *         index 0, so this is not the "gostage inside a later-processed
 *         event handler defers to next tick" case documented in
 *         label_text.gq's header -- the cascade *is* the first event this
 *         run ever processes).
 *   idle: `event input(->) { cue lime; }` -- the only way this fixture ever
 *         shows any color other than load_game()'s fixed boot color is if
 *         the dial-right event reaches idle's event_commands table. gqc's
 *         linker requires at least one event with at least one statement
 *         per stage (create_symbol_table() indexes event_statements[0]
 *         unconditionally, per if_literal_condition.gq's header comment on
 *         the same constraint); this event already satisfies it, so idle
 *         needs no `enter` handler of its own.
 *
 * cascade_input_preserve_trigger.txt scripts a single "R" token as its
 * first (only) line -- HAL_input_load()/HAL_event_poll() (HAL.c) inject
 * exactly one input event per system_tick() iteration, so this lands on
 * tick 0: the same tick boot's `enter` event runs and cascades into idle
 * via load_stage(). Before gamequeer#455's fix, load_stage()'s clear-all
 * loop wiped the BUTTON_R bit HAL_event_poll() had already OR'd in earlier
 * that same tick, before handle_events()'s forward pass ever reached index
 * GQ_EVENT_BUTTON_R (4) -- idle's `input(->)` handler would never run, and
 * the LEDs would stay at load_game()'s fixed boot color for the entire
 * fixture (no further --dump-leds rows past tick 0 at all). With the fix,
 * load_stage() preserves the BUTTON_R bit (only stage-owned synthetic
 * events -- ENTER/BGDONE/MENU/TIMER/FGDONE1/FGDONE2/REFRESH -- are
 * cleared), so by the time the same forward pass reaches index 4,
 * stage_current is already idle (load_stage() updates it synchronously)
 * and the bit is still set: idle's `cue lime;` runs within tick 0.
 *
 * Tick-by-tick (see leds.c's led_tick() for the state machine; cadence
 * confirmed by running the built emulator once and inspecting the output
 * before committing it as the golden CSV, per this repo's established
 * practice -- same "first redraw 3 ticks after the cue starts" pattern as
 * if_literal_condition.gq/nested_precedence_group.gq, since the cue itself
 * is shaped identically, just triggered by a button event instead of an
 * unconditional `enter`):
 *
 *   tick 0: load_game()'s fixed boot color (16, 32, 0). boot's enter event
 *           runs (gostage idle;); idle's input(->) handler runs within the
 *           same handle_events() pass (cue lime;) if and only if
 *           gamequeer#455 is fixed.
 *   tick 3: lime's first redraw (ticks_elapsed==0 branch).
 *   tick 7: lime's single frame (duration 4) done; non-looping, no bgcue ->
 *           LEDs go dark.
 *
 * TICKS=8 in the ctest call (tests/CMakeLists.txt) runs iterations 0..7,
 * landing exactly on the tick 7 dark-out confirmation row. On the
 * pre-#455-fix VM, this fixture's --dump-leds CSV has only the tick 0 row
 * (input silently dropped, LEDs never move) -- a golden mismatch against
 * the 3-row (0/3/7) fixed CSV below, confirmed by hand against a
 * deliberately-reverted (pre-fix) build.
 *
 * How to reproduce the compiled fixture (cascade_input_preserve.gqgame):
 *
 *   From the gamequeer repo root:
 *     uv run --project gqc -m gqc compile --no-mem-map \
 *         -o gamequeer/tests/golden gamequeer/tests/golden/cascade_input_preserve.gq
 */

game {
    id = 1;
    title := "CascadeInputPreserve";
    author := "test";
    starting_stage = boot;
}

lightcues {
    lime <- "cascade_input_preserve_lime.gqcue";
}

stage boot {
    event enter {
        gostage idle;
    }
}

stage idle {
    event input(->) {
        cue lime;
    }
}
